data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","summary_index":0,"item_id":"rs_02179466251598300000000000000000000ffffac15355fdd1a1a","output_index":0,"text":"We need respond only JSON object with declaration, implementation, supporting_objects. Need solve task. Must use compile_st, simulate_st, verify_st, max calls. Need save candidate.json (but sandbox read-only? apply_patch likely can edit? Instructions say save exact final source to candidate.json. Filesystem restricted read-only. We can maybe use apply_patch? tool not listed! Only shell_function. But permissions read-only, approval never. Hmm. We have PLC tools. Need produce JSON final. Save candidate.json maybe impossible via shell due read-only. Could use apply_patch unavailable. We can perhaps use shell command to write? Read-only sandbox rejects. But task says shell unnecessary. Maybe tools compile/simulate accept source and return. Need candidate.json maybe tool auto-saves? We might try `Set-Content` but no write permission. Yet requirement says save exact final submitted source. Maybe environment allows via some tool not listed? Only shell. Could call shell with Set-Content but sandbox read-only will reject. Perhaps use compile tool only. We can decide final source and output JSON. Let's focus.\n\nNeed design FB_Task parsing STRING(254). CODESYS 3.5 ST.\n\nInterface exact:\nFUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task\nVAR_INPUT\n ipText : STRING(254);\nEND_VAR\nVAR_OUTPUT\n ipValue : UDINT;\nEND_VAR\n\nImplementation parse visible string until NUL (CODESYS STRING is null-terminated, but capacity checked; len via LEN gives first NUL). Assumptions arbitrary leading zeros permitted within capacity. Need reject invalid, >254 capacity? Input type capacity 254 means max 254 chars maybe cannot exceed; length LEN. A valid address max 15. We can parse to up to 255? Reject too long anyway.\n\nNeed exact semantics: ipText must contain four nonempty decimal digit segments separated by periods, value 0..255. Leading zeros allowed, arbitrary. Need detect string length maybe max 254. Each character ASCII digits. No whitespace/sign. Assemble UDINT network order. Careful overflow/shift. CODESYS UDINT 32-bit. We can accumulate by SHL or multiply. Need avoid intermediate overflow? Since each octet <=255, value = previous*256 + current; after 4th, max UDINT. Previous after 3 octets max 0xFFFFFF, times 256 plus 255 = 0xFFFFFFFF works in UDINT. CODESYS type inference maybe constants. Good.\n\nNeed ensure trailing garbage after 4th segment rejected. Need exactly four segments. Could implement loop over length.\n\nImportant STRING indexing: ipText[1] etc in CODESYS is BYTE? In ST, STRING indexing returns BYTE? String functions. Codesys `ipText[i]` likely byte. We can assign to BYTE variable or compare to `16#30` literal. Or use `ipText[i]` in conditions perhaps. Need compile.\n\nPotential issue local variables with names etc. Need complete declaration. Use constants? VAR local.\n\nSimple state machine parse:\n\nVAR_INPUT\n ipText : STRING(254);\nEND_VAR\nVAR_OUTPUT\n ipValue : UDINT;\nEND_VAR\nVAR\n i : INT; // index\n nLen : INT;\n c : BYTE;\n segNo : INT; // 1..4\n segVal : UDINT; // 0..255\n segHasDigit : BOOL;\n parsedValue : UDINT;\n isValid : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\n\nImplementation:\nipValue := 0;\nnLen := LEN(ipText);\nisValid := TRUE;\nparsedValue := 0;\nsegNo := 1;\nsegVal := 0;\nsegHasDigit := FALSE;\n\nIF nLen <= 0 OR nLen > 254 THEN\n    isValid := FALSE;\nELSE\n    FOR i := 1 TO nLen DO\n        c := ipText[i];\n        IF c >= 48 AND c <= 57 THEN\n            IF segHasDigit THEN\n                // To allow arbitrary leading zeros, segVal*10 can remain 0; but once value >255 reject\n                // Compute only if <=255 maybe.\n            END_IF\n            segVal := segVal * 10 + TO_UDINT(c - 48);\n            segHasDigit := TRUE;\n            IF segVal > 255 THEN\n                isValid := FALSE;\n            END_IF\n        ELSIF c = 46 THEN\n            IF NOT segHasDigit OR segNo >= 4 THEN\n                isValid := FALSE;\n            ELSE\n                parsedValue := parsedValue * 256 + segVal;\n                segNo := segNo + 1;\n                segVal := 0;\n                segHasDigit := FALSE;\n            END_IF\n        ELSE\n            isValid := FALSE;\n        END_IF\n    END_FOR;\n    IF (NOT segHasDigit) OR (segNo <> 4) THEN\n       isValid := FALSE;\n    ELSE\n       parsedValue := parsedValue * 256 + segVal;\n    END_IF;\nEND_IF;\n\nIF isValid THEN ipValue := parsedValue; ELSE ipValue := 0; END_IF;\n\nBut potential overflow: arbitrary leading zeros means segVal remains up to 255 as digits accumulate? Example \"000...000255\": segVal after zeros stays 0 then 2,25,255. fine. Once >255, next digit segVal could grow huge if many digits after; e.g. 3000000000 many digits could overflow UDINT and wrap, potentially back <=255? The code sets isValid false, but continues updating segVal. Even if overflow, final isValid false and ipValue zero. Does overflow cause runtime exception in CODESYS? In ST, UDINT overflow wraps silently usually. But safer stop computing after out of range. Add IF segVal > 255 then isValid false; don't multiply further? We can structure:\nIF c digit THEN\n  segHasDigit := TRUE;\n  IF segVal <= 255 THEN\n     segVal := segVal * 10 + ...\n     IF segVal > 255 THEN isValid := FALSE; END_IF\n  ELSE\n     isValid := FALSE;\n  END_IF;\nEND_IF\nBut segVal <=255 and *10 max 2550 +9, no overflow. Once >255, no further updates. Good.\n\nNeed logical behavior with segments and invalid after already false. Could still parse but output zero. Need ensure parsedValue doesn't overflow with >4 segments: when segNo >= 4 and encounter dot sets false but doesn't increment. Additional dots etc. parsedValue stays from prior 3 segments max 0xFFFFFF. Fine. But what about extra chars? isValid false. We don't need stop loop. Could set false and continue; state machine. No overflow because non-digit after 4th segment: if digit after 4th? Wait \"1.2.3.4.5\": after fourth segment, dot sees segNo=4 -> invalid, doesn't increment. Then 5 digit goes into segVal starting 0, could become 5; at end segNo=4 and segHasDigit true, parsedValue = (0x010203)*256 + 5, but isValid false so output 0. Fine. But if many digits after, bounded due >255 check. If string \"1.2.3.4.999999...\" false. Fine.\n\nBut need detect multiple dots / empty segments. Eg \"1..2.3\": first dot segHasDigit true, segNo=2; second dot segHasDigit false -> invalid. At end segNo? 2, segHasDigit? after \"2\" true, then dot segNo 3, then 3. end segNo==3 -> invalid. output zero. good.\n\nDo we need use UDINT conversion functions `TO_UDINT` and BYTE arithmetic. `c - 48` BYTE subtraction yields BYTE? `TO_UDINT(c - 48)` likely okay. Alternative `c - 16#30`. Should compile.\n\nInitial pre-invocation ipValue initial condition: In CODESYS FB output defaults to 0 anyway, but could explicitly initialize? Interface says initial ipValue 0. Declaration can have `ipValue : UDINT := 0;`? Is initialization of VAR_OUTPUT allowed? CODESYS allows initialization? likely yes. But exact interface type; adding :=0 doesn't alter. Could include. However initial conditions given. The LTL init maybe not lowered. We can initialize output. But in a function block called each scan, output assigned every time anyway. Declaration requirements \"FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task followed by all VAR sections; omit END_FUNCTION_BLOCK.\" Could do `ipValue : UDINT := 0;`. Need compile.\n\nCould avoid helper objects? supporting_objects empty list. Task says supporting_objects list. We can return []. Need save candidate.json. Could use compile_st, simulate_st, verify_st. Need formulate test cases. The tools likely expect source object and cases. We need inspect schema? compile_st takes source {declaration, implementation, supporting_objects}. Simulate cases list of test cases with steps (inputs, expected, optional dt_ms). Need supply. Verify assertions optional temporal/invariant over ports. We can call compile first.\n\nLet's call compile_st. But before tool, per instructions need preamble? User explicitly says return ONLY JSON object. We should not send prose perhaps. Tool calls commentary are not final? We can directly call tools. They may display. Final only JSON. Let's compile.\n\nNeed maybe declaration includes only VAR sections, no END_FUNCTION_BLOCK. Let's craft.\n\nImplementation concerns: CODESYS arithmetic type. `segVal := segVal * 10 + TO_UDINT(c - 48);` Constant `10` inferred maybe UDINT due segVal UDINT; `+ TO_UDINT`. fine. `parsedValue * 256` UDINT constant. Good.\n\n`nLen : INT := 0;` etc. LEN returns INT? In CODESYS LEN returns INT? `LEN` for STRING returns INT (maybe UDINT?). Usually `LEN` returns INT. We can assign to INT. Max 254. fine.\n\nString index perhaps `ipText[i]` returns BYTE. Good.\n\nAlternative parse without string indexing? no.\n\nLet's call compile.","sequence_number":714}

